{"id": "EUVD-2026-93308", "enisaUuid": "c8d49395-a9f3-383d-b63b-80dbc42fd98d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/siw: Bound fragmented header copies by the remaining length\n\nsiw_get_hdr() can receive an extended DDP/RDMAP header across more than\none TCP callback. The first callback may receive most of the header,\nwhile the next one still limits the copy to hdrlen - MIN_DDP_HDR instead\nof the number of missing bytes. This makes the destination move past the\nend of the header and overwrite the receive state, including\nfpdu_part_rcvd. A later callback can then use a negative fpdu_part_rcvd\nvalue as a copy offset, which creates an OOB write.\n\nUse the number of header bytes already received when calculating the\nnext copy length.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:46:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:17:33", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2c6fbcf4bfac0b2b186acc8d91154c0fa24468a7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/af9f5b474a260ad23ffb9793d716a5e3bbce3b48", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/262dcd809723723ed8a4e05437ec7e9c21a8f17e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eb4d7a946970469b3ab0c762432bf161d5b0836c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8628f8ebf41669302513fb3f0bf0eba38b226742", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b72dcfb9bf1f0f0147cda03dc59e4002a315067f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e6bdfdf3bcb02d0d626a45e8c98b7e63d2fddf9d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9ff797e516dbc1ecb73701ec4c24055712d44411"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98323", "GHSA-6mmc-6x3m-rgjh"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.56, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1549546f-23f3-309d-9aee-bac4d8fc5eb4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "1a648435-1da6-327f-9d3b-3c77b3eb7ee6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "pat